silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_02_typed_source_signature_sections_02_operations_as_typed_arrows_concrete_anchor_11#taxonomycatusstring silm:hasLongDescription "The TaxonomyCatusString is the bare taxonomic epithet catus (Felis catus TSN 183798); a taxonomy-source leg, not Mittens. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'catus', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
